# The ledger of `llm/anthropic`: what the official SDKs of Claude's API let a
# program do with the Messages API, one block per capability, and what Rebel
# answers. No standard library speaks the API, so the yardstick is the
# census the coordinator set on 2026-11-17: Anthropic's official SDKs for
# Python and Go. Measured on this machine on 2026-11-18: Python's
# `anthropic` 2.10.0, installed with `pip --target` into the scratch folder
# and walked with `dir()` from a client (`python3 -I`), and Go's
# `github.com/anthropics/anthropic-sdk-go/v2` v2.11.0, from a module cache
# in the scratch folder (`go doc -all`, the package and `option`). Anthropic
# publishes no Rust SDK, so every `rust` line is `-`. The behaviour is the
# API reference's (platform.claude.com/docs, read 2026-11-18: Create a
# Message, Streaming, Tool use, Handle tool calls, Stop reasons, Token
# counting, Batch processing, Models, Errors, Rate limits, API versions),
# tested against answers and event streams replayed by a server of the
# tests' own on the loopback; no test reaches the API, and the one live
# test runs only with a key of its own in `REBEL_ANTHROPIC_LIVE_KEY`.

capability client/key  a client made with an API key, sent as `x-api-key`
  heroes  llm/anthropic.default_client, llm/anthropic.Client
  go      anthropic.NewClient, option.WithAPIKey
  rust    -
  python  Anthropic, Anthropic.api_key
  note    Two retries, ten minutes an attempt, as both SDKs default

capability client/env  the key and the address read from the environment
  heroes  llm/anthropic.client_from_env
  go      anthropic.DefaultClientOptions, option.WithEnvironmentProduction
  rust    -
  python  Anthropic (reads ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN, ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL)
  note    The OAuth profiles on disk and workload identity federation the SDKs also resolve are refused below

capability client/auth-token  an OAuth access token sent as `Authorization: Bearer`
  heroes  llm/anthropic.Client
  go      option.WithAuthToken
  rust    -
  python  Anthropic.auth_token, Anthropic.auth_headers

capability client/base-url  another address: a proxy, a gateway, a test's server
  heroes  llm/anthropic.Client
  go      option.WithBaseURL
  rust    -
  python  Anthropic.base_url

capability client/headers  fields added to every request, and betas named
  heroes  llm/anthropic.Client
  go      option.WithHeader, option.WithHeaderAdd, option.WithHeaderDel, option.WithQuery, option.WithQueryAdd, option.WithQueryDel
  rust    -
  python  Anthropic.default_headers, Anthropic.default_query, Anthropic.platform_headers, Anthropic.user_agent, Anthropic.with_options
  note    A beta is a name in `Client.betas`, sent as `anthropic-beta`; a query is the path's own in `send_raw`

capability client/retries  a request sent again after a transient failure, waiting what the server asks
  heroes  llm/anthropic.Client
  go      option.WithMaxRetries
  rust    -
  python  Anthropic.max_retries
  note    408, 409, 429 and 5xx and a connection that failed, unless `x-should-retry` says otherwise, as both SDKs; a `retry-after` longer than `max_wait_ms` is told to the program in its failure rather than slept, where the SDKs fall back to their own backoff

capability client/timeout  a time limit on an attempt, and on the wait for a stream's next bytes
  heroes  llm/anthropic.Client
  go      option.WithRequestTimeout, anthropic.CalculateNonStreamingTimeout
  rust    -
  python  Anthropic.timeout
  note    A stream is bounded by its silence, never by its length, so a long answer streams whole

capability client/transport  the authorities trusted, the connection's own settings
  heroes  llm/anthropic.Client
  go      option.WithHTTPClient
  rust    -
  python  DefaultHttpxClient, DefaultAsyncHttpxClient, DefaultAioHttpClient, DEFAULT_CONNECTION_LIMITS
  note    The connection is `http`'s over `tls`; `roots` names other authorities, and nothing turns the check off

capability messages/create  a message made from a conversation, its answer read whole
  heroes  llm/anthropic.create
  go      MessageService.New
  rust    -
  python  messages.create

capability messages/request  the request: the model, the ceiling of tokens, the system prompt, and every other parameter by name
  heroes  llm/anthropic.Request, llm/anthropic.new_request, llm/anthropic.with_field, llm/anthropic.with_effort, llm/anthropic.to_json
  go      MessageNewParams, OutputConfigParam, ThinkingConfigParamUnion, ToolChoiceUnionParam, MetadataParam, option.WithJSONSet, option.WithJSONDel
  rust    -
  python  messages.create's parameters, types.MessageCreateParams
  note    A parameter the record does not type is a `json.Value` by its name, so one the API adds needs nothing here; temperature, top_p and top_k are refused by the version itself

capability messages/turns  the turns of a conversation, the user's and the assistant's
  heroes  llm/anthropic.Turn, llm/anthropic.user, llm/anthropic.assistant, llm/anthropic.with_turn
  go      MessageParam, NewUserMessage, NewAssistantMessage
  rust    -
  python  types.MessageParam

capability messages/blocks-in  the content blocks a request sends: text, image, PDF
  heroes  llm/anthropic.text_block, llm/anthropic.image_block, llm/anthropic.document_block
  go      NewTextBlock, NewImageBlock, NewDocumentBlock, TextBlockParam, ImageBlockParam, DocumentBlockParam, Base64ImageSourceParam, Base64PDFSourceParam
  rust    -
  python  types.TextBlockParam, types.ImageBlockParam, types.DocumentBlockParam
  note    Every other block (a URL's image, a file's id, a search result) is the JSON the reference writes, a `json.Value` in `Turn.content`

capability messages/cache-control  the end of a prefix the API caches, for five minutes or an hour
  heroes  llm/anthropic.cached
  go      CacheControlEphemeralParam, NewCacheControlEphemeralParam
  rust    -
  python  types.CacheControlEphemeralParam

capability messages/answer  the answer read: id, model, content, stop, usage
  heroes  llm/anthropic.Message, llm/anthropic.Usage, llm/anthropic.to_message, llm/anthropic.parse_message
  go      Message, Usage, Message.UnmarshalJSON, Message.RawJSON
  rust    -
  python  types.Message, types.Usage

capability messages/blocks-out  the answer's blocks read by their kind
  heroes  llm/anthropic.Block, llm/anthropic.blocks_of, llm/anthropic.text_of
  go      ContentBlockUnion, ContentBlockUnion.AsText, AsThinking, AsRedactedThinking, AsToolUse, AsServerToolUse, AsWebSearchToolResult, AsWebFetchToolResult, AsAny
  rust    -
  python  types.ContentBlock, types.TextBlock, types.ThinkingBlock, types.RedactedThinkingBlock, types.ToolUseBlock, types.ServerToolUseBlock, MessageStream.get_final_text
  note    A server tool's result is `other` with its JSON whole: its shapes change with each tool's version

capability messages/stop  why the answer stopped, checked before its content
  heroes  llm/anthropic.STOP_END_TURN, llm/anthropic.STOP_MAX_TOKENS, llm/anthropic.STOP_STOP_SEQUENCE, llm/anthropic.STOP_TOOL_USE, llm/anthropic.STOP_PAUSE_TURN, llm/anthropic.STOP_REFUSAL, llm/anthropic.STOP_CONTEXT_WINDOW, llm/anthropic.require_complete
  go      StopReason, StopReasonEndTurn, StopReasonMaxTokens, StopReasonStopSequence, StopReasonToolUse, StopReasonPauseTurn, StopReasonRefusal, RefusalStopDetails
  rust    -
  python  types.StopReason, types.RefusalStopDetails
  note    A refusal is `permission` and a cut answer `limit` in `require_complete`; neither SDK turns them into failures, so the program that reads `stop_reason` itself reads the same values

capability messages/replay  an answer sent back as the assistant's turn, its thinking unchanged; a paused turn continued
  heroes  llm/anthropic.turn_of, llm/anthropic.with_reply
  go      Message.ToParam, ContentBlockUnion.ToParam
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    The blocks go back as the API wrote them, so a thinking block's signature is never rebuilt

capability tools/define  a tool of the program's: name, description, input schema, strict, eager streaming; and a server tool
  heroes  llm/anthropic.Tool, llm/anthropic.Request
  go      ToolParam, ToolUnionParam, ToolInputSchemaParam, WebSearchTool20250305Param
  rust    -
  python  types.ToolParam, types.ToolUnionParam, transform_schema
  note    A server tool is its JSON in `Request.server_tools`; a schema is JSON the program writes, there being no reflection to derive one from a record

capability tools/calls  the calls of an answer handed out to the program
  heroes  llm/anthropic.tool_calls_of, llm/anthropic.ToolCall
  go      ToolUseBlock, ContentBlockUnion.AsToolUse
  rust    -
  python  types.ToolUseBlock

capability tools/input-checked  a call's input checked whole before it is used
  heroes  llm/anthropic.input_of
  go      ToolUseBlock.Input
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    Both SDKs parse the streamed input tolerantly and may hand out a silent truncation; here the text as it came is kept and `input_of` fails `invalid` on anything that is not one whole object

capability tools/results  the results of one turn's calls sent back in one user turn, an error marked
  heroes  llm/anthropic.tool_result, llm/anthropic.with_tool_results
  go      NewToolResultBlock, ToolResultBlockParam
  rust    -
  python  types.ToolResultBlockParam

capability tools/runner  a loop that calls the program's functions until the model is done
  heroes  refused: the program drives the loop; a library that calls back would need a closure for each tool's state, which the language has not, and the loop is six lines (the example of `with_tool_results`)
  go      toolrunner.NewBetaToolFromJSONSchema, BetaMessageService.NewToolRunner, BetaToolRunner.RunToCompletion
  rust    -
  python  beta_tool, beta_async_tool, beta.messages.tool_runner

capability streaming/events  a message read as its events come, every kind of event
  heroes  llm/anthropic.stream, llm/anthropic.next_event, llm/anthropic.Event, llm/anthropic.Stream
  go      MessageService.NewStreaming, ssestream.Stream, MessageStreamEventUnion
  rust    -
  python  messages.stream, messages.create(stream=True), MessageStream, Stream, MessageStreamEvent, TextEvent, InputJsonEvent, ContentBlockStopEvent, MessageStopEvent
  note    An event this package does not name is `other`, as the versioning page asks; an `error` event is a failure with the status its type stands for

capability streaming/accumulate  the message a stream makes, whole or as far as it has come
  heroes  llm/anthropic.final_message, llm/anthropic.message_of
  go      Message.Accumulate
  rust    -
  python  MessageStream.get_final_message, MessageStream.current_message_snapshot, MessageStream.until_done

capability streaming/partial-input  a tool's input read while it streams
  heroes  llm/anthropic.input_so_far
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  InputJsonEvent.snapshot
  note    Read by `json.parse_partial`, which guesses nothing: a key or a word not yet whole is left out

capability streaming/close  a stream closed before or after its end
  heroes  llm/anthropic.close_stream
  go      ssestream.Stream.Close
  rust    -
  python  MessageStream.close, Stream.close

capability tokens/count  the input tokens a request would cost, counted by the API
  heroes  llm/anthropic.count_input_tokens
  go      MessageService.CountTokens, MessageTokensCount
  rust    -
  python  messages.count_tokens

capability models/list  a page of the models the API serves
  heroes  llm/anthropic.list_models, llm/anthropic.first_page, llm/anthropic.Cursor, llm/anthropic.ModelPage
  go      ModelService.List, pagination.Page
  rust    -
  python  models.list

capability models/retrieve  one model by its id, its context window and its ceiling
  heroes  llm/anthropic.model_of, llm/anthropic.ModelInfo, llm/anthropic.to_model_info
  go      ModelService.Get, ModelInfo
  rust    -
  python  models.retrieve, types.ModelInfo

capability pages/auto  every page of a list walked for the program
  heroes  refused: the program's loop over `has_more` and `last_id` is two lines, and an iterator would need a closure
  go      ModelService.ListAutoPaging, MessageBatchService.ListAutoPaging, pagination.PageAutoPager
  rust    -
  python  SyncPage iteration, Anthropic.get_api_list

capability batches/create  requests sent as one batch, each named
  heroes  llm/anthropic.create_batch, llm/anthropic.BatchRequest, llm/anthropic.Batch, llm/anthropic.RequestCounts, llm/anthropic.to_batch
  go      MessageBatchService.New, MessageBatch, MessageBatchRequestCounts
  rust    -
  python  messages.batches.create, types.MessageBatch

capability batches/retrieve  a batch polled until it ends
  heroes  llm/anthropic.batch_of, llm/anthropic.BATCH_IN_PROGRESS, llm/anthropic.BATCH_CANCELING, llm/anthropic.BATCH_ENDED
  go      MessageBatchService.Get
  rust    -
  python  messages.batches.retrieve

capability batches/list  a page of the batches
  heroes  llm/anthropic.list_batches, llm/anthropic.BatchPage
  go      MessageBatchService.List
  rust    -
  python  messages.batches.list

capability batches/cancel  a batch cancelled
  heroes  llm/anthropic.cancel_batch
  go      MessageBatchService.Cancel
  rust    -
  python  messages.batches.cancel

capability batches/delete  an ended batch deleted
  heroes  llm/anthropic.delete_batch
  go      MessageBatchService.Delete, DeletedMessageBatch
  rust    -
  python  messages.batches.delete

capability batches/results  a batch's results read a line at a time, each found by its name
  heroes  llm/anthropic.batch_results, llm/anthropic.parse_batch_results, llm/anthropic.to_batch_result, llm/anthropic.BatchResult, llm/anthropic.Outcome
  go      MessageBatchService.ResultsStreaming, MessageBatchIndividualResponse, jsonl.Stream
  rust    -
  python  messages.batches.results, types.MessageBatchIndividualResponse
  note    The results are read from the batch's own path, never from `results_url`, so they go only where the key goes

capability errors/status  a failure the API answered, by its status and its type
  heroes  llm/anthropic.INVALID, llm/anthropic.PERMISSION, llm/anthropic.NOT_FOUND, llm/anthropic.LIMIT, llm/anthropic.TIMEOUT, llm/anthropic.FAILED, llm/anthropic.ApiError, llm/anthropic.failure_of
  go      Error, Error.StatusCode, Error.RawJSON
  rust    -
  python  APIError, APIStatusError, BadRequestError, AuthenticationError, PaymentRequiredError, PermissionDeniedError, NotFoundError, ConflictError, RequestTooLargeError, UnprocessableEntityError, RateLimitError, InternalServerError, OverloadedError, ServiceUnavailableError, GatewayTimeoutError, DeadlineExceededError, RequestTimeoutError, ContentTooLargeError
  note    Each status chooses a code of README § A4 and the message keeps the status, the type, the request id and the wait in brackets, as `sql`'s failures keep a SQLSTATE; `failure_of` reads them back

capability errors/advice  whether a failure may pass if sent again, and after how long
  heroes  llm/anthropic.ApiError
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  RetryableError
  note    `retryable` and `wait_ms` from the status, `x-should-retry` and `retry-after` (seconds or a date, through `retries.parse_retry_after`); the SDKs keep this inside their retry loop

capability errors/request-id  the id of a request, for support
  heroes  llm/anthropic.ApiError
  go      option.WithResponseInto
  rust    -
  python  MessageStream.request_id, APIStatusError.request_id

capability errors/connection  a connection refused, cut or timed out
  heroes  llm/anthropic.CLOSED, llm/anthropic.TIMEOUT
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  APIConnectionError, APITimeoutError

capability raw/request  any endpoint reached with the client's key, version and retries, its answer whole with its fields
  heroes  llm/anthropic.send_raw
  go      Client.Execute, Client.Get, Client.Post, Client.Put, Client.Patch, Client.Delete, option.WithResponseInto, option.WithResponseBodyInto, option.WithRequestBody
  rust    -
  python  Anthropic.get, Anthropic.post, Anthropic.put, Anthropic.patch, Anthropic.delete, Anthropic.request, Anthropic.with_raw_response, Anthropic.with_streaming_response
  note    The rate-limit fields (`anthropic-ratelimit-*`) are read from the answer's headers

capability structured-output  an answer held to a JSON schema and read as JSON
  heroes  llm/anthropic.with_field, json.parse
  go      OutputConfigParam, JSONOutputFormatParam
  rust    -
  python  messages.parse, types.ParsedMessage
  note    `output_config.format` is set by `with_field` and the text read by `json.parse`; filling a record from it by its field names is refused, the language having no reflection (`json`'s own rule)

capability clouds  Claude on Bedrock, Vertex AI, Foundry and Claude Platform on AWS, each with its cloud's own signing
  heroes  refused: a cloud's signing (SigV4, Google's credentials, Entra ID) is that cloud's package; `base_url` and `headers` reach a gateway that signs
  go      bedrock.NewMantleClient, vertex.WithGoogleAuth
  rust    -
  python  AnthropicBedrock, AnthropicBedrockMantle, AnthropicVertex, AnthropicFoundry, AnthropicAWS, AnthropicGoogleCloud, AsyncAnthropicBedrock, AsyncAnthropicBedrockMantle, AsyncAnthropicVertex, AsyncAnthropicFoundry, AsyncAnthropicAWS, AsyncAnthropicGoogleCloud

capability credentials/federated  credentials from OAuth profiles on disk, or exchanged by workload identity federation
  heroes  refused: an OAuth flow is `oauth2`'s, and the token it answers is `Client.auth_token`
  go      option.WithFederationTokenProvider, option.WithProfile, option.WithConfig, option.WithConfigQuiet, option.WithoutEnvironmentDefaults
  rust    -
  python  AccessToken, AccessTokenAuth, AccessTokenProvider, AsyncAccessTokenProvider, BaseURLBoundProvider, CredentialResult, CredentialsFile, EnvToken, IdentityTokenFile, IdentityTokenProvider, InMemoryConfig, StaticToken, TokenCache, WorkloadIdentityCredentials, default_credentials, exchange_federation_assertion, Anthropic.credentials, Anthropic.custom_auth

dropped  outside the package's area in README § A1: the Files and Skills APIs, Managed Agents, user profiles, the Admin API and the legacy Text Completions, each reached by `send_raw` where a program wants it
  go      FileService, OrganizationAPIKeyService and the Organization services, BetaAgentService, BetaSessionService, BetaEnvironmentService, BetaVaultService, BetaDeploymentService, BetaMemoryStoreService, BetaSkillService, UserProfileService, CompletionService
  rust    -
  python  files, skills, completions, beta.agents, beta.deployment_runs, beta.deployments, beta.dreams, beta.environments, beta.files, beta.memory_stores, beta.models, beta.organization, beta.sessions, beta.skills, beta.tunnels, beta.user_profiles, beta.vaults, beta.webhooks, user_profiles, Anthropic.webhook_key

dropped  the beta copies of the Messages API, whose features are the same requests with a beta named: compaction, context editing, task budgets, fallbacks, message threads, cache diagnostics
  go      BetaMessageService, BetaMessageBatchService, BetaModelService
  rust    -
  python  beta.messages, BetaMessageStream, BetaMessageStreamManager, BetaAsyncMessageStream, BetaAsyncMessageStreamManager, BetaContentBlockStopEvent, BetaInputJsonEvent, BetaMessageStopEvent, BetaMessageStreamEvent, BetaTextEvent, BetaFallbackState, BetaRefusalFallbackMiddleware, ParsedBetaContentBlockStopEvent, ParsedBetaMessageStopEvent, ParsedBetaMessageStreamEvent, ParsedBetaTextEvent
  note    `Client.betas` names the beta and `with_field` sets its parameter

dropped  the plumbing of each language: async twins, contexts, option and parameter helpers, middleware, telemetry, and the sentinels of omitted values
  go      context.Context, anthropic.Bool, anthropic.Int, anthropic.Float, anthropic.String, anthropic.Time, anthropic.Opt, anthropic.Ptr, param.Opt, option.WithMiddleware, option.WithDebugLog, option.WithOpenTelemetryTraces, option.WithOpenTelemetryPropagation, option.WithOpenTelemetryConversationID, option.WithOpenTelemetryTracesContentMode, option.WithOpenTelemetryTracesMaxContentBytes, option.WithTracerProvider, option.WithWebhookKey
  rust    -
  python  AsyncAnthropic, AsyncClient, AsyncStream, AsyncMessageStream, AsyncMessageStreamManager, AsyncAPIResponse, APIResponse, APIRequest, Client, BaseModel, NotGiven, NOT_GIVEN, not_given, Omit, omit, NoneType, RequestOptions, Timeout, DEFAULT_MAX_RETRIES, DEFAULT_TIMEOUT, Middleware, MiddlewareCallable, MiddlewareInput, AsyncMiddlewareCallable, CallNext, AsyncCallNext, OpenTelemetryClientOption, OpenTelemetryOptions, OpenTelemetryTraces, ResolvedOpenTelemetryOptions, ResolvedOpenTelemetryTraces, MessageStreamManager, Anthropic.copy, Anthropic.close, Anthropic.is_closed, Anthropic.middleware, Anthropic.with_middleware, Anthropic.open_telemetry, Anthropic.qs, file_from_path, lib, pagination, resources, types, transform_schema

dropped  failures of the SDKs' own machinery or of other surfaces, which a program of this package meets as a status's code
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  AnthropicError, APIResponseValidationError, APIWebhookValidationError, CredentialsError, IdentityTokenFileError, WorkloadIdentityError, CMEKContextUnavailableError, CMEKKeyDisabledError, CMEKKeyNetworkBlockedError, CMEKKeyUnreachableError, ClaudeCodeKeyCreatorNotMemberError, ClaudeCodeVersionTooOldError, ClientClosedRequestError, ContractSpendLimitReachedError, EnforcedSpendLimitReachedError, HTTPNotImplementedError, LinkedOrganizationBillingUnavailableError, LinkedOrganizationSpendLimitReachedError, OrganizationOnHoldError, OrganizationTypeNotSupportedError, ParentOrganizationRequiredError, PreconditionFailedError, RampLimitExceededError, RequestBodyEncodingInvalidError, RequestBodyEncodingUnsupportedError, RequestBodyTooLargeAfterDecodingError, RequestHeaderFieldsTooLargeError, SandboxEgressRestrictedError
